  "Description": {
    "Cost": 1159893,
    "UIName": "Shadow Hawk LAM",
    "Id": "chassisdef_shadowhawk_lam_SHD-X1",
    "Name": "Shadow Hawk LAM",
    "Details": "The original and considerably flawed prototypes were completed in 2680. Based on the Shadow Hawk SHD-2H, the 'Mech carried a Class 2 Autocannon in place of the Class 5. The SHD-X1 carried only 6.5 tons of armor for protection. Only one chassis survived multiple crashes caused by its faulty schematics. It had a top ground speed of 86.4 km/h like its progenitor, the SHD-2H, and used ten single heat sinks. Field refits to increase firepower with wing-mounted weapons were common, but often caused more problems than they solved.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Land Air Mech</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.05</color></b>",
